# Local Toolchain — Development Machines (template)

Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` and fill in the paths of your own machines.
`CLAUDE.local.md` is listed in `.gitignore` and is never committed: absolute
paths, user names and a tool inventory of a private machine do not belong in a
published repository.

Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.local.md` alongside `CLAUDE.md`, so whatever you put
here is available as context without being published.

Record per machine only what is not derivable from the repository:

## <Platform> (<role: build / verification / …>)

- `lazbuild`: `<full path>` (note it here when it is not on `PATH`)
- mORMot2 sources: `<full path>`
- Target: `<cpu-os>`
- Build workarounds this machine needs (missing development symlinks,
  linker flags, …)
- Available for checking output: `<tools>`
- Missing: `<tools>`, and what you substitute for them
